// std/rational.dag -- Rational numbers (ℚ) as a field over the integers.
//
// Layer 4 of the construction chain authored in
// `docs/design-numeric-construction.md`:
//
//   Magnitude → Nat → Int → Rational → Real
//
// `Rational = Field<Int>` says "ℚ inhabits Field over the abstract integer
// algebra Int." The construction-chain progression consumes the now-canonical
// `Int = AbelianGroup<GroupCompletion<Nat>>` from Slice 3 (#1466) as the
// underlying algebra; `Field<T>` extends the ring structure with a
// multiplicative inverse and division.
//
// CONSUMERS: none in this slice. Per design doc §6 (cascade slice), legacy
// consumers continue to use the `Float`-backed surface; refinement syntax
// (`Rational<N>` for bounded precision) is gated on T-V2-Retirement.
//
// HARD BOUNDARIES (per dispatch on inbox #1288 #4362611659):
//   - No NonZero/result reciprocal semantics introduced here. Director's
//     dispatch explicitly defers this: "Do not implement NonZero/result
//     reciprocal semantics in this PR unless review proves the current
//     `Field<T>` surface cannot be used without it."
//   - No refinement syntax.
//   - No consumer migration.
//
// EXECUTABLE-COMPLETENESS GAP (P5 tracked scaffold):
//   `Field<T>` at `dsl/std/algebra.dag:240` declares `reciprocal: fn(T) -> T`.
//   Under the standard parametric reading, `T = Int` types
//   `reciprocal: fn(Int) -> Int` — denotationally false: ℤ has only ±1 as
//   units, so reciprocal is undefined for every other integer (0 included).
//   The honest field-of-fractions construction would be
//   `Rational = Field<FieldOfFractions<Int>>` where `FieldOfFractions<R>`
//   is a derived-carrier opaque atom (analogous to `GroupCompletion<M>` from
//   #1448; the carrier whose elements all have multiplicative inverses, with
//   zero handled per the field axioms).
//
//   Prior `Field` verification audit (#1370) acknowledged this completeness
//   gap and deferred the reciprocal/division refinement work. This slice
//   continues that posture: the alias declaration is denotationally
//   correct *under the field-of-fractions interpretation* (ℚ = field of
//   fractions of ℤ); the substrate cannot yet express that interpretation
//   structurally without a parallel carrier.
//
//   **Dissolution trigger:** when the substrate gains either
//   (a) a `FieldOfFractions<R>` opaque atom (mirroring the GroupCompletion
//       precedent — separate substrate-introduction slice), or
//   (b) NonZero/Result-shaped reciprocal/division refinement,
//   sharpen this declaration to the structurally-honest form. Existing
//   `type Rational = Field<Int>` use sites continue to type-check because
//   the new form is a stricter refinement of the same algebra.
//
//   **Mitigation in this slice:** the structural ratchet pins `Rational`
//   resolving to `Field<Int>` exactly — making the denotational
//   interpretation observable as a use-site fact. If reviewers prove the
//   parametric reading is too lossy here (mirroring the AbelianGroup<Nat>
//   M9 precedent), the slice escalates to Director for substrate-split
//   ratification, same as the GroupCompletion path for Slice 3.

module std.rational

import std.algebra { Field }
import std.integer { Int }

type Rational = Field<Int>
